  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay) proposes a utility that excludes selected windows from screen sharing, recording and screenshots, using a hotkey in the style of Always on Top. PowerToys#48566 asks for the same thing, including always masking chosen apps such as Teams and Outlook by name, and was closed as a duplicate of #46333. The feature is not yet available in PowerToys. Please subscribe to #46333 and add a thumbs-up reaction to follow progress. A proof-of-concept exists there that uses a hook DLL with SetWindowDisplayAffinity, and the maintainers are still deciding where the feature should live. Until it ships, share a single app window instead of the whole screen, or check the screen before you share."
